om the lab machines of the late 1960s to the containers and cloud hosts of today.\n\n`ls` belongs to the first generation of Unix userland programs written at Bell Labs. Ken Thompson and Dennis Ritchie, working on a PDP-7 and then a PDP-11, needed a way to inspect the directories their new filesystem produced. Early Unix treated a directory as a special file whose contents were names paired with inode numbers. Listing those names was not a shell"}}}}], "reply": {"configOptions": [{"id": "model", "name": "Model", "category": "model", "type": "select", "currentValue": "amazon-bedrock/us.xai.grok-4.7", "options": [{"value": "amazon-bedrock/us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6", "name": "amazon-bedrock/Claude Sonnet 4.6 (US)"}, {"value": "amazon-bedrock/us.xai.grok-4.7", "name": "amazon-bedrock/Grok 4.7 (US)"}, {"value": "amazon-bedrock/us.moonshotai.kimi-k3", "name": "amazon-bedrock/Kimi K3 (US)"}, {"value": "opencode/big-pickle", "name": "opencode/Big Pickle"}, {"value": "opencode/tidepool-alpha-free", "name": "opencode/Tidepool Alpha Free"}]}, {"id": "effort", "name": "Effort", "description": "Available effort levels for this model", "category": "thought_level", "type": "select", "currentValue": "default", "options": [{"value": "low", "name": "Low"}, {"value": "medium", "name": "Medium"}, {"value": "high", "name": "High"}, {"value": "xhigh", "name": "Xhigh"}, {"value": "default", "name": "Default"}]}, {"id": "mode", "name": "Session Mode", "category": "mode", "type": "select", "currentValue": "build", "options": [{"value": "build", "name": "Build", "description": "The default agent. Executes tools based on configured permissions."}, {"value": "plan", "name": "Plan", "description": "Read-only agent for exploring the codebase and planning work before implementation."}]}]}}
